Innerclasses
An Inner Class is a class declared inside another class.
Syntax
Syntax
class Outer {

    class Inner {

    }
}
Why do we use an Inner Class?

We use an inner class when one class is closely related to another class and doesn't make sense to exist independently.

Example

Think of a Car and its Engine.

An Engine belongs to a Car.
It doesn't usually exist independently in your program.
Example1
class Outer {

    int x = 100;

    class Inner {

        void display() {
            System.out.println(x);
        }
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Outer outer = new Outer();

        Outer.Inner inner = outer.new Inner();

        inner.display();
    }
}
output
100
Example2
class Mobile {

    String brand = "Samsung";

    class Battery {

        void show() {
            System.out.println("Battery belongs to " + brand);
        }
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Mobile mobile = new Mobile();

        Mobile.Battery battery = mobile.new Battery();

        battery.show();
    }

}
output
Battery belongs to Samsung

Types of Inner Classes
1. Member Inner Class
class A {

    class B {

    }
}

Most commonly used.

2. Static Inner Class
class Car {

    static String company = "BMW";

    static class Engine {

        void start() { //normal method
            System.out.println("Engine Started");
            System.out.println("Company : " + company);
        }
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Car.Engine engine = new Car.Engine();

        engine.start();
    }
}
output
Engine Started
Company : BMW



3. Local Inner Class

Class inside a method.

class A {

    void show() {

        // Local Inner Class (inside method)
        class B {

            void display() {
                System.out.println("Hello from Local Inner Class");
            }
        }

        // object create inside method
        B b = new B();
        b.display();
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A obj = new A();
        obj.show();
    }
}
output
Hello from Local Inner Class
Example
A class = Office
 show() = Meeting
B class = Temporary helper person once that role is finished that time its deleted
4. Anonymous Inner Class

A class with no name, used only once.

