Anonymous Class

What is Anonymous Class in Java?

An Anonymous Class is a class that does NOT have a name and is created at the same time while creating an object.
“Class without name + used only once”
Why do we use Anonymous Class?

We use it when:

We need a class only one time
We want to override a method quickly
We don’t want to create a separate .java class file

